    {
      "cost": "reaction",
      "name": "Resist Reality",
      "section": "defensive",
      "text": "**Trigger** The warpstitcher would take damage

---

**Effect** The warpstitcher gains resistance 12 to the triggering damage type until the start of their next turn. The resistance applies to the triggering damage.",
      "traits": [
        "occult",
      ],
    },
    {
      "cost": 2,
      "name": "Fold Reality",
      "section": "offensive",
      "text": "The warpstitcher collapses the space between themself and another location. They choose a 10-foot square within 120 feet. The warpstitcher then Strides, treating the chosen area as adjacent to them.",
      "traits": [
        "concentrate",
        "occult",
      ],
    },
    {
      "cost": null,
      "name": "Threads of Quintessence",
      "section": "offensive",
      "text": "The warpstitcher's claws are laced with strands of quintessence they force into victims' wounds. This functions as Grab, or Improved Grab on a critical hit.",
      "traits": [],
    },
    {
      "cost": 1,
      "name": "Warp Suture",
      "section": "offensive",
      "text": "**Requirements** The warpstitcher has a creature {{condition: Grabbed}} or {{condition: Restrained}}

---

**Effect** The warpstitcher sews the creature into themself. The creature is pulled into the warpstitcher's space and moves with the warpstitcher. It becomes restrained and takes ::dice[3d12] force damage at the end of each of its turns until freed. Additionally, it takes ::dice[1d12] force damage whenever the warpstitcher uses Resist Reality (DC 34 basic Will save). The Escape DC is 34 (Escape), or the sutures can be severed (AC 25, Hardness 8, HP 30, weakness to slashing 5), freeing the creature. The warpstitcher can have up to 12 Bulk of creatures sewn into their body. The body of a creature that dies while sutured is absorbed into the warpstitcher's body and destroyed ::button[1d4 rounds | 1d4] later.",
      "traits": [
        "manipulate",
      ],
    },
  ],
  "createdAt": "",
  "description": "Warpstitchers are self-proclaimed guardians of existence, holding the belief that they were created by the gods to sew together the space between alternate realities. These horrifying aberrations relentlessly hunt anything they suspect abuses magic or technology to change the fabric of the multiverse. Once they find their quarry, they wait only long enough to confirm their suspicions before attacking. Potential threats—a neophyte spellcaster trying their first cantrips, an academic theorist exploring interstellar travel—instead earn a telepathic warning of what awaits should they pursue their efforts too far. Everything other than threats (potential or otherwise) is a possible tool, a target for warpstitcher lies and coercion.

Their mere appearance is fuel for nightmares, with insectile limbs supporting a massive, bulbous torso. From their back spring five multi-segmented limbs ending in wicked claws threaded with the very stuff of reality that they use to skewer their prey, who they then sew into their bodies. Such unfortunate creatures quickly dissolve, possibly sustaining the warpstitchers, though whether that's through their flesh, thoughts, or alternate reality potential is unknown. Those few who survive are plagued by disturbing, haunting visions; a smaller percentage instead see visions of happier possible lives, gaining peace and sometimes unprecedented witchwarper powers.",
